salem-robotics-inc|PHYS||Strong|PHYS_EVAL|Robots that perceive and act on their own inside cluttered, hazardous facilities|autonomy in unstructured industrial sites = perception stack -> P2|Manipulation policies that generalize across facilities they were never trained in are the hard part of autonomous site work.
mireye|PHYS|P4|Moderate|RAG|Building a queryable model of real-world places for AI agents|grounding agents in physical-world data = vision and world modeling -> P2|Fusing street imagery, maps and listings into one consistent place graph is harder than the search layer on top.
cosmic-robotics|PHYS||Strong||Autonomous construction robots working on unstructured terrain|terrain perception and autonomy -> P2|Excavation autonomy depends on terrain perception that holds up as dust, lighting and soil conditions change.
robocurve|PHYS_EVAL||Strong|PHYS|Reproducible benchmarks that score robot policies on real jobs|robot policy evals = VLA/perception work plus eval harnesses -> P2+P3|Reproducible robot evals need sim-to-real parity, which most published benchmarks never achieve.
hilstart|PHYS_EVAL|P6|Moderate|SEARCH|AI agents that test and debug physical hardware|physical agent harness = evaluation of embodied agents -> P2+P3|Closing the loop between an agent's actions and real instrument readings is the bottleneck in autonomous hardware testing.
hub|PHYS_EVAL||Moderate|PHYS|Real-world multimodal training data for frontier labs and robotics|robot training data -> P2+P3|Egocentric data only helps robot policies when capture setups match the target embodiment and tasks.
spaceflow-technologies-inc|GENERIC||None|RAG|Automating procurement for physical-goods businesses|procurement operations, no matching technical proof point|Supplier quotes arrive in every format, so normalizing line items is the core extraction problem in procurement automation.
rise-reforming|GENERIC||None||Chemical process that turns waste gases into chemicals|process chemistry, no ML proof point|Catalyst stability under variable waste-gas composition decides whether a reforming process survives outside the lab.
insforge-instacloud|GENERIC||None|CODE|Serverless cloud that coding agents deploy to directly|cloud infrastructure; coding-agent overlap is indirect|Coding agents ship broken backends when the platform gives them no structured runtime feedback on what failed.
enjamb-labs|RAG|P3|Moderate|AGENT_EVAL|AI agents for biopharma work over regulated documents|life-science work runs over large regulated document sets -> P4|Biopharma agents fail when retrieval misses the one protocol amendment or SOP version that governs the answer.
arden|RAG||Moderate|AGENT_EVAL|Agents that pull and test internal audit evidence|audit evidence spread across many documents = retrieval -> P4|Audit agents must trace every control test to the exact evidence document, which is a retrieval precision problem.
arzana|RAG||Moderate|AGENT_EVAL|Extracting quotes and orders from manufacturers' operational data|models over messy operational documents -> P4|Parsing free-form RFQs and purchase orders into ERP fields is where manufacturer automation loses accuracy.
flowscope|AGENT_EVAL||Moderate||Deploying agents that automate business processes reliably|process automation agents need quality systems -> P3|Process automation agents need regression tests on real process traces before every change ships.
characterquilt|AGENT_EVAL||Moderate|CODE|Computer-use agents that deploy enterprise marketing campaigns|computer-use agents need eval harnesses -> P3|Computer-use agents break on UI drift in ad platforms, so replayable evals on real campaign flows matter most.
tasklet-2|AGENT_EVAL||Strong||General agents that own real work across many tools|long-horizon agents across tools need evals -> P3|Long-running agents drift over multi-day tasks, so trajectory-level evaluation matters more than scoring single responses.
tolmo|CODE||Moderate|AGENT_EVAL|Agents that secure code, CI and cloud applications|agentic review of code and CI -> P3 coding|Security agents reviewing code and CI need very low false-positive rates or developers mute them within a week.
testerarmy|CODE||Strong|AGENT_EVAL|AI agent that tests web and mobile apps|testing agents = coding-agent quality -> P3|Test agents lose trust fast when flaky UI assertions outnumber real regressions in their reports.
bloom-4|CODE||Moderate||Coding agents that build cross-platform mobile apps|vibe-coding tool = coding agents -> P3|Generated mobile apps break on native builds, so agent output needs device-level checks before users see it.
andco|LEGAL||Strong|RAG|Agents that gather and synthesize records for personal injury cases|legal record synthesis for law firms -> P4+P5|Injury case records run thousands of pages, and a missed treatment gap changes case value.
general-legal|LEGAL||Strong||AI law firm for high-growth companies|law firm AI over legal documents -> P4+P5|An AI law firm depends on retrieving the right precedent and clause language across a growing matter library.
stilta|LEGAL||Strong||Agentic AI for patent litigation|prior art retrieval over huge patent corpora -> P4+P5|Invalidity search means finding prior art across millions of patents whose wording differs from the claims.
discovered-materials|SEARCH||Moderate||AI scientists that discover semiconductor materials|candidate search against expensive simulations -> P6|Materials agents spend most compute on slow DFT runs, so choosing which candidates to simulate decides throughput.
luminal|SEARCH||Moderate|GENERIC|ML compiler that generates fast GPU code|search over kernel schedules against slow hardware measurements -> P6|Compiler search over GPU kernel schedules is bounded by how many candidates you can benchmark on real hardware.
idler|SEARCH|P3|Strong|AGENT_EVAL|Hill-climbing benchmarks for frontier models across domains|search and optimization against expensive evaluations -> P6|Benchmark hill-climbing is bounded by eval cost, so choosing which runs to spend compute on decides progress.
structured-ai|DIAGRAM||Strong||AI review of architecture and engineering drawing packages|engineering drawings -> P7|Cross-referencing details and callouts across sheets of a drawing set is where automated QA/QC gets hard.
monarcha|DIAGRAM||Moderate||Turning maps into structured georeferenced data|digitizing maps and plans -> P7|Historic mining maps use inconsistent projections and hand annotations that break automated georeferencing.
artifact-2|DIAGRAM||Moderate|SEARCH|Collaborative AI IDE for hardware engineers|schematics and engineering diagrams -> P7|Hardware design review depends on reading schematics and block diagrams as structured data.
